speechtext:
Madam Speaker, pursuant to Standing Order 41(2), I wish to table the following documents, in both official languages:
1.	Order in council PC 1980-2915 issued pursuant to subsection 35(1) of the Petroleum Administration Act, as well as the proclamation declaring the coming into force of division II of part II of the said act;
2.	Order in council PC 1980-2916 issued under section 36 of the Petroleum Administration Act, as well as the regulations prescribing maximum prices for crude oil;
3.	Order in council PC 1980-2917 issued pursuant to section 52(2) of the Petroleum Administration Act, as well as the proclamation declaring that subsection 52(1) of the said act shall come into force on November 1, 1980;
4.	Order in council PC 1980-2918 issued pursuant to subsection 52(1) of the Petroleum Administration Act, as well as the 1980 regulations prescribing prices for natural gas;
5.	Order in council PC 1980-2919 issued pursuant to section 62 of the Petroleum Administration Act, as well as the amendment to part III regulations of the Petroleum Administration Act;
6.	Order in council PC 1980-2920 issued pursuant to subsection 72(4) of the Petroleum Administration Act.
In order to give members of the House easy access to those documents, I would be willing, if it is agreeable to the House, to move that the orders be printed as an appendix to today's Hansard.

Short Title
1.	These Regulations may be cited as the Natural Gas Prices Regulations, 1980.
Interpretation
2.	(1) In these Regulations,
"cost of transportation" of natural gas moved from one place to another, means the aggregate of the costs of transmission and metering and all other costs associated with such movement of natural gas;
"imputed Alberta border price" of natural gas produced, extracted or recovered in the Province of Alberta and delivered to the border of that Province means 177.565 cents per gigajoule;
"international border price" of natural gas produced, extracted or recovered in the Province of Alberta and delivered at various points on the international boundary line between Canada and the United States for consumption outside Canada means the Canadian dollar equivalent, calculated in accordance with the conditions of the applicable licence, of
(a)	417 cents in United States currency per gigajoule, with respect to natural gas exported under the authority of Licence No. GL-1, GL-3, GL-4, GL-5, GL-6, GL-16, GL-17, GL-18, GL-19, GL-20, GL-24, GL-25, GL-28, GL-35, GL-36, GL-37, GL-38, GL-39, GL-41, GL-43, GL-52, GL-54, GL-55, GL-57, GL-60 or GL-61; and
(b)	340 cents in United States currency per gigajoule, with respect to natural gas exported under the authority of Licence No. GL-29.
(2) Each zone referred to in the schedule is an area of Canada comprising a zone proposed by TransCanada PipeLines Limited in its application to the National Energy Board dated August 14, 1969 and approved with modifications by the National Energy Board by Order No. TG-1-73 of May 10, 1973.
Prescription
3.	the prices for natural gas produced in the Province of Alberta that enters into interprovincial trade for sale in Canada outside Alberta are, in Canadian currency, as follows:
(a)	for natural gas sold by TransCanada PipeLines Limited for consumption in Canada in a zone set out in Column 1 of the schedule, the aggregate of the imputed Alberta border price and the transportation rates set out opposite that zone in the column of that schedule that is applicable to the type of service under which the gas is sold;
(b)	for natural gas consumed by TransCanada PipeLines Limited as fuel or for other uses, including any gas lost during transmission, the imputed Alberta border price;
(c)	for natural gas sold by TransCanada PipeLines Limited to ICG Transmission Limited at Spruce, in the Province of
November 12, 1980
Manitoba, for export under Licence No. GL-28, the international border price less the cost of transportation on the ICG Transmission Limited pipeline from Spruce to the international boundary between Canada and the United States of America near Sprague, in the Province of Manitoba, which cost is a monthly demand charge of 3,209 dollars;
(d)	for natural gas sold by TransCanada PipeLines Limited to ICG Transmission Limited at Spruce, in the Province of Manitoba, for export from Canada and re-import into Canada under Licence No. GL-30 and for subsequent reexport from Canada under Licence No. GL-29 at Fort Frances, in the Province of Ontario, the international border price less the aggregate of
(i)	the cost of transportation on the ICG Transmission Limited pipeline in Canada, which cost is a monthly demand charge of 59,678 dollars,
(ii)	the cost of transportation on the Inter-City Minnesota Pipelines Ltd. pipeline in the United States, which cost, in United States currency, is a monthly demand charge of 13,190 dollars, and
(iii)	a commodity charge of 0.171 cents per cubic metre delivered.
(e)	for natural gas sold
(i)	by TransCanada PipeLines Limited to Niagara Gas Transmission Limited for export under Licence Nos. GL-6 and GL-55,
(ii)	by TransCanada PipeLines Limited to The Consumers' Gas Company, which gas is subsequently sold by The Consumers' Gas Company to Niagara Gas Transmission Limited for export under Licence No. GL-6, and
(iii)	by The Consumers' Gas Company to Niagara Gas Transmission Limited under an agreement dated October 31, 1975 between those two companies,
the international border price for gas exported under those licences less the cost of transportation on the Niagara Gas Transmission Limited pipeline from Cornwall to the international boundary between Canada and the United States near Cornwall, such cost being the average cost of transportation calculated in accordance with the contract dated January 2, 1968 made between Niagara Gas Transmission Limited and St. Lawrence Gas Company Inc. and approved by the National Energy Board;
(/) for natural gas sold by Many Islands Pipe Lines (Canada) Limited to Saskatchewan Power Corporation at the point of interconnection of the facilities of these two companies near Beacon Hill, in the Province of Saskatchewan, which cost is a monthly demand charge of 1.959 cents per cubic metre for 1048.1 thousand cubic metres of daily demand;
(g)	for natural gas sold by Many Islands Pipe Lines Limited to the Saskatchewan Power Corporation at the point of interconnection of the facilities of Mid-Continent Pipe Lines Limited and the facilities of the Saskatchewan Power Corporation near Hatton in the Province of Saskatchewan, the aggregate of the imputed Alberta border price and 0.00088 cents per cubic metre, being the cost of transportation on
that portion of the Mid-Continent pipeline in the Province of Saskatchewan;
(h)	for natural gas sold by Many Islands Pipe Lines Limited and Saskatchewan Power Corporation to TransCanada Pipelines Limited at Success, in the Province of Saskatchewan, the aggregate of the imputed Alberta border price and
0.126 cents per cubic metre, being the cost of transportation on that portion of the Mid-Continent pipeline in the Province of Saskatchewan and on the facilities of the Saskatchewan Power Corporation pipeline connecting with those of TransCanada Pipelines Limited;"
(/) for natural gas sold by Consolidated Natural Gas Limited to TransCanada PipeLines Limited at a point in the Province of Saskatchewan near Burstall, the imputed Alberta border price;
U) natural gas sold by Consolidated Natural Gas Limited to Greater Winnipeg Gas Company at a point in the Province of Saskatchewan near Burstall, the imputed Alberta border price;
(k) for natural gas sold by Pan-Alberta Gas Ltd., to Gaz Metropolitain, Inc. at a point in the Province of Saskatchewan near Burstall, the imputed Alberta border price;
(/) for natural gas sold by Many Islands Pipe Lines Limited to Saskatchewan Power Corporation at a point in the Province of Saskatchewan near Merid, the imputed Alberta border price;
(m) for natural gas sold by Alberta and Southern Gas Co. Ltd. to Columbia Natural Gas Limited at various points of connection between the facilities of Alberta Natural Gas Company and Columbia Natural Gas Limited in the Province of British Columbia, the aggregate of the imputed Alberta border-price and the average cost of transportation in the Province of British Columbia to the various delivery points on the Alberta Natural Gas Company pipeline, incurred during the month of the sale of the gas and calculated in accordance with Order No. TG-1-80, issued by the National Energy Board;
(«) for natural gas sold by Westcoast Transmission Company Limited to Columbia Natural Gas Limited at various points of connection between the facilities of Alberta Natural Gas Company and Columbia Natural Gas Limited in the Province of British Columbia, the aggregate of the imputed Alberta border price and the average cost of transportation in the Province of British Columbia to the various delivery points on the Alberta Natural Gas Company pipeline, incurred during the month of the sale of the gas and calculated in accordance with Order No. TG-1-80, issued by the National Energy Board;
(o) for natural gas sold by Alberta and Southern Gas Co. Ltd. to Inland Natural Gas Co. Ltd at the point of connection of the facilities of Alberta Natural Gas Company and those of Inland Natural Gas Co. Ltd. in the Province of British Columbia near Yahk, the aggregate of
(i)	the imputed Alberta border price,
(ii)	a peaking service charge in respect of the volumes
delivered in each month equal to thirty per cent of the
price paid by Alberta and Southern Gas Co. Ltd. to
November 12, 1980
acquire that gas in the Province of Alberta in each month from the Alberta Petroleum Marketing Commission, and
(iii)	the cost of transportation in the Province of British Columbia on the Alberta Natural Gas Company pipeline, incurred during the month of the sale of the gas and calculated in accordance with Order No. TG-1-80, issued by the National Energy Board;
(p) for natural gas sold by Alberta and Southern Gas Co. Ltd. to Westcoast Transmission Company Limited at a place on the international boundary between Canada and the United States near Kingsgate, in the Province of British Columbia, the international border price;
(,q) for natural gas sold as peaking service gas by Trans-Canada PipeLines Limited to Niagara Gas Transmission Limited at Cornwall, in the Province of Ontario, for export under Licence No. GL-6, 15.497 cents per cubic metre plus the aggregate of the transportation commodity rate and the transportation demand rate for Contract Demand service in the Eastern Zone as specified in Schedule 1 and the imputed Alberta border price;
(/[DOT]) for natural gas sold by Many Islands Pipe Lines (Canada) Limited to Saskatchewan Power Corporation at the point of interconnection of the facilities of those two companies near Smiley, in the Province of Saskatchewan, the aggregate of the imputed Alberta border price and the cost of transportation on that portion of the Many Islands Pipe Lines (Canada) Lmited pipeline between the Alberta Saskatchewan border and Smiley, Saskatchewan, which cost is a monthly demand charge of 0.035 cents per cubic metre for 481.6 thousand cubic metres of daily demand;
($) for natural gas sold after October 31, 1976, by Many Islands Pipe Lines (Canada) Limited to Saskatchewan Power Corporation at the point of interconnection of the facilities of Many Islands Pipe Lines (Canada) Limited and the facilities of Saskatchewan Power Corporation near Unity, in the Province of Saskatchewan, the aggregate of the imputed Alberta border price and the cost of transportation on that portion of the Many Islands Pipe Lines (Canada) Limited pipeline in the Province of Saskatchewan, which cost is a monthly demand charge of 0.522 cents per cubic metre for 835.7 thousand cubic metres of daily demand;
(/) for natural gas sold by Alberta and Southern Gas Co. Ltd. to Westcoast Transmission Company Limited at the point of connection of the facilities of Alberta Natural Gas Company and those of Inland Natural Gas Co. Ltd. near Yahk, in the Province of British Columbia, for export under Licence No. GL-41, the international border price less 0.600 cents per cubic metre, being the cost of transportation on the Westcoast Transmission Company Limited and Inland Natural Gas Co. Ltd. pipelines from Yahk to the international boundary line between Canada and the United States of America near Huntingdon, in the Province of British Columbia;
(u)	for natural gas sold as fuel by Alberta and Southern Gas Co. Ltd. to Westcoast Transmission Company Limited
under an agreement dated January 17, 1977 between those two companies for delivery at the point of connection of the facilities of Alberta Natural Gas Company and those of Inland Natural Gas Co. Ltd. near Yahk, in the Province of British Columbia, the aggregate of the imputed Alberta border price and the cost of transportation in the Province of British Columbia on the Alberta Natural Gas Company pipeline, incurred during the month of the sale of the gas and calculated in accordance with Order No. TG-1-80, issued by the National Energy Board;
(v)	for natural gas sold by TransCanada PipeLines Limited to Gaz Metropolitain, Inc. at the point of connection of the facilities of those two companies near Montreal, in the Province of Quebec, for export f.o.b. Gaz Metropolitain, Inc.'s liquefaction plant in the City of Montreal, under Order No. GO-2-80 issued by the National Energy Board, the international border price for gas exported under Licence No. GL-19;
(w)	for natural gas sold by TransCanada PipeLines Limited to Saskatchewan Power Corporation at Unity, in the Province of Saskatchewan, under an agreement dated the 30th day of June, 1972, as amended, between those two companies, the imputed Alberta border price;
(x)	for natural gas sold by TransCanada PipeLines Limited to Gaz Metropolitain Inc. at the point of connection of the facilities of TransCanada PipeLines Limited and those of Gaz Metropolitain Inc. near Montreal, in the Province of Quebec, under an agreement dated February 15, 1977 between TransCanada PipeLines Limited and Gaz Metropolitain Inc. and approved by the National Energy Board, the aggregate of the imputed Alberta border price and the transporation commodity rate for Contract Demand service in the Eastern Zone as specified in the schedule;
(y)	for natural gas sold by Pan-Alberta Gas Ltd. to Sulpetro Limited at a point in the Province of Saskatchewan near Burstall, for export under Licence No. GL-57, the international border price for gas exported under that Licence, less the cost of transportation on the TransCanada PipeLines Limited system in respect of the volumes delivered in each month for export under that Licence, which cost shall be based on the monthly demand rate and the transportation commodity rate per cubic metre of natural gas delivered as set out in the schedule to the Sulpetro Limited Export Price Order, and
(z)	for natural gas sold by TransCanada PipeLines Limited to Consolidated Natural Gas Limited at a point in the Province of Saskatchewan near Burstall, for export under Licence No. GL-61, the international border price for gas exported under that Licence, less the cost of transportation on the TransCanada PipeLines Limited system in respect of the volumes delivered in each month for export under that Licence, which cost shall be based on the monthly demand rate and the transportation commodity rate per cubic metre of natural gas delivered as set out for Licence No. GL-61 in Schedule I to the TransCanada PipeLines Limited Export Price Order.
